From 3800ff84c3ee8337b558fa380687f1e757d9a703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:52:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 110/274] TileLang V4.1: name every kernel after its file and
 what it computes

TileLang names a CUDA kernel after its prim_func, and most of ours were
called main, so every profile and SASS dump showed main_kernel and kernels
had to be told apart by grid. Each prim_func is now <file>_<what>, or the
file's own name for a file's single kernel (gemm_bf16_splitk_kernel,
mhc_project_streams_kernel, moe_combine_kernel, vocab_packed_projection_kernel,
metadata_decode_kernel, ...), so a profile line names the module that holds
it. Variants a factory builds share its name.

The TileLang L2 prefetch moves from glm5next/nvidia/l2_prefetch_tilelang.py
to glm5next/nvidia/tilelang/l2_prefetch.py (kernel l2_prefetch), the same
family-directory layout as deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/; its test follows. Only
symbols and that path change; the generated code and the results are the
same.

